  "terrainName": "basic-desert",
  "description": "What: the breath's release gates on a dragon (CE-3490 BA-6, F-9 Protocol III). On basic-desert three dragons (TKB 411, 60 m up at x 100) each attack the first man of a row of three hostile riflemen at x 400: 'Held Dragon' the Held Men (y 188\u2026212) with a neutral 'Civilian' standing 1.5 m beside Held Man 1 (400, 189.5); 'Control Dragon' the same row with no civilian (y 438\u2026462); 'Forbidden Dragon' (its ROE forbids incendiaries) the Forbidden Men (y 688\u2026712). Judge: the Held Dragon holds its breath while the civilian is inside the flame it would throw (DESIGN_Breath_Attack \u00a77: the hold is the burn cone) and the civilian is never hurt; the Control Dragon burns its row and Control Man 1 dies; the Forbidden Dragon never breathes and its men are never hurt."
 },
